 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a69c67d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Basic Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2146b035",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(url)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8da89bb2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Visual check"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7d92244",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "You'll learn this properly on Day 5 with visualization\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4e84ec3f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For now, use describe() and percentile logic"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c87734a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"Fare\"].describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dde79506",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# IQR method — the standard statistical approach"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7b5f9e26",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Q1 = df[\"Fare\"].quantile(0.25)\n",
    "Q3 = df[\"Fare\"].quantile(0.75)\n",
    "IQR = Q3 - Q1\n",
    "\n",
    "lower = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR\n",
    "upper  = Q3 + 1.25 * IQR"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b8f6a8d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Find outliers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "10df87f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "outliers = df[(df[\"Fare\"] < lower) | (df[\"Fare\"] > upper)]\n",
    "print(f\"{len(outliers)} Outliers Found!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe6b9d9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Options: drop them, cap them, or keep and note them\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "69730a71",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Capping (Winsorization) — replace outliers with the boundary value"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ac077910",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"Fare\"] = df[\"Fare\"].clip(lower=lower , upper=upper)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c7ad974",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For your EDA project, don't always drop outliers. First understand them — a fare of 512 on Titanic might be a real first-class suite. Document your decision."
   ]
  }
 ],
